{"kind":"stack","id":"s-materials","title":"Changes that make new materials","theme":{"background":"#fdf6e3","foreground":"#073642","font":"Georgia, serif"}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c1","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c1-q","content":"When you burn a piece of paper, what happens to it?"},{"type":"button","id":"c1-a","label":"It turns into new materials, like ash and smoke","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-b","label":"It just gets wet and soft","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c1-c","label":"It turns back into a tree","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c2"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c2","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c2-t","content":"Irreversible change"},{"type":"text","id":"c2-e","content":"A change that is very hard or impossible to undo. Once new materials form, they usually cannot turn back into the original materials."},{"type":"button","id":"c2-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c3"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c3","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c3-q","content":"Which of these is a change that makes a new material?"},{"type":"button","id":"c3-a","label":"Baking a cake in the oven","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-b","label":"Folding a sheet of paper","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c3-c","label":"Melting an ice cube in your hand","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c4"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c4","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c4-t","content":"You mix vinegar, an acid, with bicarbonate of soda in a cup. It fizzes! What do you do next?"},{"type":"button","id":"c4-a","label":"Feel the cup to see if it is warm","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c5"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c4-b","label":"Pour the fizzing mixture onto a tray to see what is left","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c6"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c5","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c5-t","content":"The cup is warm. The fizzing made new materials, and the change released heat. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c5-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c6","kind":"story","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c6-t","content":"The tray holds a new white powder. The mixture has changed into new materials and cannot easily be turned back. Well done!"},{"type":"button","id":"c6-n","label":"Continue","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c7"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c7","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c7-q","content":"Why is it hard to turn new materials back into the original ones?"},{"type":"button","id":"c7-a","label":"New materials form, so the change is irreversible","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-b","label":"New materials always melt back into water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c7-c","label":"New materials are always lighter than before","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c8"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c8","kind":"flash","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c8-t","content":"Bicarbonate of soda"},{"type":"text","id":"c8-e","content":"A white powder. When it mixes with an acid such as vinegar, it fizzes and makes new materials."},{"type":"button","id":"c8-n","label":"Next Card","actions":[{"type":"goto","cardId":"c9"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c9","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c9-q","content":"What do you see when bicarbonate of soda meets vinegar?"},{"type":"button","id":"c9-a","label":"Fizzing and bubbles","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-b","label":"Nothing at all happens","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c9-c","label":"The mixture turns solid ice","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c10"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c10","kind":"quiz","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c10-q","content":"Which change is usually irreversible?"},{"type":"button","id":"c10-a","label":"Burning wood in a fire","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":1},{"type":"sound","sound":"cheer"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-b","label":"Dissolving sugar in water","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]},{"type":"button","id":"c10-c","label":"Stretching an elastic band","actions":[{"type":"score","delta":0},{"type":"sound","sound":"buzz"},{"type":"goto","cardId":"c11"}]}],"actions":[]}}
{"kind":"card","card":{"id":"c11","kind":"end","elements":[{"type":"text","id":"c11-t","content":"Well done! You finished the lesson on changes that make new materials."},{"type":"text","id":"c11-m","content":"Keep looking for changes around you. Ask yourself: is something new being made, and could it be turned back?"}],"actions":[]}}
